<HandoverLayout title="Maintainer handover" description="The operational handover for the OPDA knowledge base, model toolchain, working-group services and supporting content." overview>
  <h1>Maintainer handover</h1>
  <p class="lead">A practical guide to taking responsibility for the OPDA knowledge base, its semantic-model toolchain and the services around it. Start with access and a reproducible build, then complete the service and ownership checks before accepting the handover.</p>
  <p><strong>Repository review:</strong> <time datetime="2026-10-26">26 October 2026</time>. <strong>Document status:</strong> public operational reference; acceptance remains to be recorded by the receiving owner.</p>

  <Callout title="What this handover establishes" tone="important">
    <p>The commands and architecture below are grounded in the checked-in implementation. A template, passing test or historic receipt does not prove that an account is accessible, an automation is running or an integration is enabled today. Those checks are listed explicitly. This page does not certify a completed transfer or approve a standard.</p>
    <p>Account identifiers, tenant locations, private submissions, personal contact details, credentials and recovery secrets belong in an authorised, restricted handoff. Obtain access through OPDA's owners; do not place those details in this public page or Git history.</p>
  </Callout>

